It should not print a second > before a textarea that follows an inline element
<div><label for="x">Name</label><textarea id="x" rows="4"></textarea></div>

It should not print a second > before a textarea at a wide print width
printWidth: 200
<div><label for="x">Name</label><textarea id="x" rows="4"></textarea></div>

It should not print a second > before a textarea at a very wide print width
printWidth: 9999
<div><label for="x">Name</label><textarea id="x" rows="4"></textarea></div>

It should not print a second > before a textarea that follows a void element
<div><img src="a"><textarea>hi</textarea></div>
